Body:
Hey @myerspat not sure if you're aware, but UM just recently updated their API. The existing stuff I think is still working for now, though will be deprecated in the near future, but now their API is much closer to current OpenAI standards. You'll need to create a new API key at the self service portal that is linked here:
https://its.umich.edu/computing/ai/gpt-toolkit-in-depth

After that I was able to successfully add UM GPT to opencode with this as the configuration (they have a bunch of other available models as well, this is just including one as an example):
```
"provider": {
	"UMGPT": {
	    "npm": "@ai-sdk/azure",
	    "name": "UM GPT",
	    "options": {
		"baseURL": "https://api.toolkit.umgpt.umich.edu/",
		"apiKey": "{env:API_KEY}",
		"headers":{
		    "Authorization": "Bearer {env:API_KEY}"
		}
	    },
	    "models": {
		"gpt-5.4": {
		    "name": "gpt-5.4",
		}
	    }
	}
```
